<title>BRAZIL: Brazil Congress panel puts off telecom bill vote.</title>
<headline>Brazil Congress panel puts off telecom bill vote.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>A bill outlining the rules for the privatization of Brazil's telecommunications sector will not be put to a vote in its Chamber of Deputies panel Tuesday as had been expected, an official said.</p>
<p>&quot;Today we will continue discussions of the bill. Voting will take place at a later date,&quot; said deputy Paulo Bornhausen, president of the committee mulling the General Telecommunications Law.  </p>
<p>If approved in the panel, the bill advances to the floor of the Chamber of Deputies and then to the Senate.</p>
<p>(( -- James Craig, Brasilia newsroom 5561 2230358))</p>
